[[File:MA13FerryDroid-TMCh8.png|thumb|right|250px|A ferry droid on Nevarro]]
'''Ferry droids''' were [[droid]]s that operated [[keelboat]]s. On the [[Magma|lava]] rivers of<ref name="Databank">{{Databank|ferry-droid|ferry droid}}</ref> the [[Volcano|volcanic]] [[planet]]<ref name="Chapter 7">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 7: The Reckoning}}</ref> [[Nevarro]], ferry droids provided safe passage for travelers.<ref name="Databank" />

One ferry droid, named [[MA-13]]<ref name="Droid Factory set">{{DisneyToyCite|set=Star Wars: Droid Factory (toy line)|packtype=Multipack|pack=R6-D3 · MA-13 · R1 · N0-AH|altlink=https://wdwnt.com/2021/12/photos-new-the-mandalorian-droid-factory-set-now-available-at-disneys-hollywood-studios}}</ref>, rowed a [[boat]] that was used by the [[Mandalorian]] [[bounty hunter]] [[Din Djarin]], the former [[shock trooper]] [[Carasynthia Dune|Cara Dune]], the [[Bounty Hunters' Guild]] operative [[Greef Karga]], and the former [[assassin droid]] [[IG-11]] to escape the pursuit of the forces of [[Moff]] [[Gideon]]'s [[Gideon's Imperial remnant|Imperial remnant]] with the [[Youngling|infant]] known as [[Din Grogu|Grogu]]. When the ferry droid refused to stop rowing the boat as it approached the exit of the lava river, where Gideon's [[stormtrooper]]s were waiting, Dune shot the droid, but was unable to halt the boat.<ref name="Chapter 8">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 8: Redemption}}</ref>

